       specifies only “an integer value other than EERRRR”) upon successful  com‐
       pletion.

       X/Open defines no error conditions.  SVr4 does document some error con‐
       ditions which apply in general:

       •   This implementation will return EERRRR on attempts to use color values
           outside  the range 00 to CCOOLLOORRSS-1 (except for the default colors ex‐
           tension), or use color pairs outside the range 00 to CCOOLLOORR__PPAAIIRRSS--11.

           Color values used in iinniitt__ccoolloorr must be in the range 00 to 11000000.

           An error is returned from all functions if  the  terminal  has  not
           been initialized.

           An  error is returned from secondary functions such as iinniitt__ppaaiirr if
           ssttaarrtt__ccoolloorr was not called.

       •   SVr4  does  much  the  same,  except  that  it  returns  EERRRR   from
           ppaaiirr__ccoonntteenntt  if  the pair was not initialized using iinniitt__ppaaiirrss and
           it returns EERRRR from ccoolloorr__ccoonntteenntt if the terminal does not  support
           changing colors.

           This implementation does not return EERRRR for either case.

       Specific functions make additional checks:

          iinniitt__ccoolloorr
               returns an error if the terminal does not support this feature,
               e.g., if the iinniittiiaalliizzee__ccoolloorr capability  is  absent  from  the
